 \"source\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"tools-evidence/neo-server-cli.txt\",\n      \"sha256\": \"c248c265b39d3c1ee75f1465324e9974d2133ca747747347e108f6ec3a81a8e1\",\n      \"mediaType\": \"text/plain\",\n      \"role\": \"source\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"neo-sidecar.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"b562fa60a28eb3b5dc53814e7c92b53f9cbae7268e1a13d8048b64a204937973\",\n      \"mediaType\": \"application/json\",\n      \"role\": \"source\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"DEFECT-01 RESOLVED upstream in a8728f79 and still fixed at cf541253: the older validator demanded a zh-CN member in the generated-locales manifest that the frozen source commit can never emit (RegisteredUiLanguage excludes zh-CN). The current validator requires only the five languages the userscript generator really writes and validates inlineChineseSources instead. No case is blocked for locale reasons.\",\n    \"DEFECT-06 (blocking for every browser case, new in cf541253): browser-focus-guard.mjs requires the owned temporary window to lie entirely outside every active display. On a single-display macOS host this is unreachable, because the WindowServer clamps normal windows so that part of the window always remains on screen. This was measured two independent ways on an owned temporary instance (CDP Browser.setWindowBounds and the Accessibility API) and both agree; see artifacts/focus/window-placement-probe.json and artifacts/focus/focus-preflight.json. The gate therefore turns into a hard stop for all 22 cases, and resume.md forbids browser operations without a running guard.\",\n    \"DEFECT-02 (blocking for 5 cases): the trusted focus-safe helper focus-safe-browser.cjs required by --focus-safe-helper exists neither in the repository nor anywhere under $HOME, and the handoff forbids fabricating it. UI-01, PRIVATE-01, PRIVATE-02, YT-01 and OCR-UI-01 depend on it.\",\n    \"DEFECT-03 (blocking for 5 cases): Playwright is absent from package.json and pnpm-lock.yaml, so --playwright-root cannot be satisfied from this checkout.\",\n    \"DEFECT-04: Chromium 151 ignores --load-extension, which the repository browser specials still pass; the unpacked build had to be loaded through CDP Extensions.loadUnpacked in the earlier part of this acceptance.\",\n    \"DEFECT-05 RESOLVED for the stdio path in this run: the BrowserOS neo control surface is no longer bound to the single daily profile. browseros-claw-server 0.0.66 accepts --config and --stdio, honours a run-local ports.cdp and directories.resources, keeps its state in BROWSERCLAW_DIR, and answered initialize/tools/list with the full 22-tool surface while the daily instance stayed untouched. The handoff still forbids pointing the HTTP path at the daily client configuration, and no browser operation was performed through the control surface because the focus guard never reached running.\",\n    \"The extended window-placement probe and the single focus preflight were run before any browser case, purely to decide whether the mandatory guard can ever certify this host. They are diagnostics, not case evidence, and they never activated, minimized, fullscreened or moved the browser onto another Space.\",\n    \"The resumed instance did not re-load the unpacked extension, because resume.md forbids browser operations without a running guard. environment.extensionId/extensionName/extensionVersion and browserExecutableSha256 are carried over from the earlier instance of the same acceptance; the product source commit, its tree and the build manifest are unchanged, so the extension identity still describes the same verified artifact, and the browser binary hash was recomputed unchanged in this run.\",\n    \"browserPid, profilePathSha256, profileMarker and launchArguments describe the resumed temporary instance; the build, locale, GPU, screenshot and browser-log artifacts carried into this record were produced earlier in the same acceptance from the previous temporary profile, which has been removed.\",\n    \"hardware.rawAdapterObservation binds the raw GPU log by file SHA-256, eventIndex, context and timestamp. hardware.adapterDescription is the raw value (Chromium 151 reports an empty GPUAdapterInfo.description) and the human-readable explanation moved to adapterLabel. The legacy GPUAdapter.isFallbackAdapter property is absent in Chromium 151; fallback state is reported on GPUAdapterInfo.isFallbackAdapter (=false).\",\n    \"GPU scope note: this is adapter discovery only, re-bound to its own raw event. No model was executed, so there is no WebGPU dispatch or graph-partition evidence, and hardware.status must not be read as inference validation.\",\n    \"No real model was downloaded or executed in this run. models[] stays empty rather than filled with unverified metadata, and every real-model case records the exact next step instead of claiming the environment cannot support it.\",\n    \"No harness script can pre-populate the fluent-read-local-models-v2 or fluent-read-manga-ocr-v1 caches, so every real-model case would additionally need product-UI-driven downloads.\",\n    \"The tested product HEAD (7212af1f9da08324963e38973c7f477aabfffb0b) is not present in this clone; the published source commit c68a53af was used and its tree was verified to equal 50e12ecc7f4c72448f03e714a585814eb9476622, as the handoff requires.\",\n    \"self-check passes and its positive samples are synthetic validator fixtures, explicitly not browser or model acceptance results.\",\n    \"Acceptance material revision: this record was produced against cf54125302be2beebb3ba8860798f3cb053a3dac (\\\"test: add guarded native Neo resume and raw GPU evidence binding\\\"), which adds resume.md, browser-focus-guard.mjs, browser-acceptance-gpu.mjs, the GPU fixture and the focus-guard schema fields, and relaxes adapterDescription to allow an empty raw string. The product source commit c68a53af and its tree 50e12ecc... are unchanged, so the extension was not rebuilt and its fingerprints still apply.\",\n    \"Generated locales were already committed in the frozen source commit; the manifestSha256 abc11522ec049930f8721119422d1808c13549061438fb08b6841fef26f48866 is unchanged because the file set did not change, and the regenerated manifest now also carries inlineChineseSources.\",\n    \"DEFECT-07 (harness robustness, observed while verifying the committed record): browser-focus-guard.mjs decides whether it is the main program with `import.meta.url === pathToFileURL(path.resolve(process.argv[1])).href` and has no else branch. On macOS /tmp is a symlink to /private/tmp, so Node resolves import.meta.url to /private/tmp/... while path.resolve(process.argv[1]) keeps the /tmp/... spelling used on the command line. Invoked through a /tmp path the script silently does nothing and still exits 0, which would let a wrapper believe the focus guard had run. Verified: `node /tmp/<archive>/scripts/testing/browser-focus-guard.mjs --self-check` printed nothing with exit 0, while the same file invoked through its /private/tmp realpath printed {ok:true,...} with exit 0.\"\n  ]\n}"
